{"id":"571702216","kind":"article","title":"灵感源泉在何方？","author":"Andy Matuschak","original_authors":["Andy Matuschak"],"original_source_urls":["https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4HpeV4MGmbKMWY6oUeci392Z7NAueHJ5WH5p"],"publisher":"Jarrett Ye","column":"常青笔记 & 知识工作","date":"2022-10-10","updated":"2026-10-28","votes":11,"comment_count":0,"minutes":2,"chars":1148,"keywords":["创造力","联想思维","注意力","长期记忆","积极情绪","创意研究"],"summary":"Andy Matuschak 汇集多项关于创意来源的笔记和研究摘要：创意可能依赖联想、注意范围和积极情绪，注意过滤较少也可能与创造性问题解决相关。正文主要以短注释串联长期记忆、实践洞见、头脑风暴和注意研究，呈现的是一组待继续探索的线索，而非完整论证。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/571702216","restoration":null,"toc":[{"id":"sec-1","level":3,"title":"队列"},{"id":"sec-2","level":2,"title":"链接至本文（已汉化）"},{"id":"sec-3","level":2,"title":"声明"}],"html":"<ul><li data-pid=\"5JcFfxTF\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z6ReihULdqZXqhY2bMACp15kwgM1sT421Cx6p\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">强大的创新往往侧重于创造全新范式，而非解决当前情境中的问题</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup><br/> </li><li data-pid=\"7308gEid\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z7YyAp683VNbTmDG4hx9QFpf5urwxZJpsycS6\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">实践出洞见</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup><br/> </li><ul><li data-pid=\"4lmkVR-Z\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3H98n8DGZmu8XArqHZVsckyWvbTe8wK4kAt2\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">有效的系统设计需要从真刀真枪的情境中汲取洞见</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup><br/> </li><li data-pid=\"Ssct4HkY\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z7Ldzn94FibghJBEG9hAebu8LMNV7NVBFvsfg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">实践出洞见时，建议摸石头过河而不是先画蓝图</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup><br/> </li></ul><li data-pid=\"ugNqTt2W\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z6cFzJWgj9vZpnrQsjrZ8yCNREzCTgyFeVZTb\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">常青笔记有助于积累洞见</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-5\"><a href=\"#ref-5\">[5]</a></sup><br/> </li><ul><li data-pid=\"5ib_-DU5\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z5cVs9BKLJsCYifhYBstAEKuZ8driDzLB3gFd\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">头脑风暴往往可以替代缺位的见解积累系统</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-6\"><a href=\"#ref-6\">[6]</a></sup><br/></li></ul><li data-pid=\"RKGv_xCZ\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zNW5jyTpU1v4XBQfTYwoM8Q\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">有些创造性的洞察力依赖于长期记忆</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-7\"><a href=\"#ref-7\">[7]</a></sup><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-8\"><a href=\"#ref-8\">[8]</a></sup><br/> </li><li data-pid=\"8RkHxtLA\">「好想法来自于多年的艰苦闲暇」；<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z5beUfpCZpi6fibB4vFfhzF\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《辞去你的工作》Wolf Tivy</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-9\"><a href=\"#ref-9\">[9]</a></sup></li></ul><h3 id=\"sec-1\">队列</h3><ul><li data-pid=\"LmD920zS\"> Mednick, S. (1962). The associative basis of the creative process. Psychological Review, 69(3), 220–232. <a class=\"external\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1037/h0048850\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"visible\">doi.org/10.1037/h004885</span><span class=\"invisible\">0</span><span class=\"ellipsis\"></span></a><br/> </li><ul><li data-pid=\"ZU08d67s\"> 本论文意在从联想的角度诠释创意性思考。<br/> </li></ul><li data-pid=\"SabjkjG8\"> Friedman, R., Fishbach, A., Förster, J., &amp; Werth, L. (2003). Attentional Priming Effects on Creativity. Creativity Research Journal - CREATIVITY RES J, 15, 277–286. <a class=\"external\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1207/S15326934CRJ152&amp;3_18\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"visible\">doi.org/10.1207/S153269</span><span class=\"invisible\">34CRJ152&amp;3_18</span><span class=\"ellipsis\"></span></a><br/> </li><ul><li data-pid=\"NXOZk9Ym\"> 作者检验了这样一个假设：感知方面注意力的范围的宽窄，对应着概念方面注意力的范围宽窄，从而会促进或阻碍创意的产生。<br/> </li></ul><li data-pid=\"a_RTOPaa\"> Rowe, G., Hirsh, J. B., &amp; Anderson, A. K. (2007). Positive affect increases the breadth of attentional selection. Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences, 104(1), 383–388. <a class=\"external\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0605198104\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"visible\">doi.org/10.1073/pnas.06</span><span class=\"invisible\">05198104</span><span class=\"ellipsis\"></span></a><br/> </li><ul><li data-pid=\"Exz1Gfg8\"> 本研究考察这样的观点：积极情绪可能有助于扩大注意力过滤机制的允许范围，降低其选择性。<br/> </li><li data-pid=\"O7M7qkam\"> 与积极情绪下广泛的注意力集中和增强的创造性问题解决相呼应，创造性智力的个体差异与注意力过滤的减少有关。例如，有创造力的人已被证明表现出较少的潜在抑制，这是对被认为不相关的刺激物的注意力下降的测量（54）。</li></ul></ul><h2 id=\"sec-2\">链接至本文（已汉化）</h2><ul><li data-pid=\"i36CHho3\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"500206391\" href=\"#/post/500206391\">知识工作者对于逐步完善想法往往没有具体方法</a></li></ul><h2 id=\"sec-3\">声明</h2><p data-pid=\"a1kSLiu9\">此内容发布由 Andy Matuschak 许可。未经允许，不得转载或修改。保留所有权利。</p><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><blockquote data-pid=\"tK_Q4Oar\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"http://paratranz.cn/projects/3131\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts Memo</a> 汉化组译制<br/>原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4HpeV4MGmbKMWY6oUeci392Z7NAueHJ5WH5p\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Where do ideas come from? (andymatuschak.org)</a></blockquote><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 强大的创新往往侧重于创造全新范式，而非解决当前情境中的问题 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"561086570\" href=\"#/post/561086570\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> 实践出洞见 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"521844479\" href=\"#/post/521844479\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-3\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-3\">↩</a> 有效的系统设计需要从真刀真枪的使用情境汲取洞见 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"552263007\" href=\"#/post/552263007\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-4\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-4\">↩</a> 实践出洞见时，建议摸石头过河而不是先画蓝图 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"484620977\" href=\"#/post/484620977\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-5\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-5\">↩</a> 常青笔记有助于积累洞见 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"448897897\" href=\"#/post/448897897\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-6\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-6\">↩</a> 头脑风暴往往可以替代缺位的见解积累系统 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"435560834\" href=\"#/post/435560834\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-7\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-7\">↩</a> 许多人认为记忆对深刻的创造性工作不重要 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"454266265\" href=\"#/post/454266265\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-8\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-8\">↩</a> 一些创新洞察依赖于长期记忆 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"677540148\" href=\"#/post/677540148\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-9\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-9\">↩</a> 《辞去你的工作》Wolf Tivy <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"676452556\" href=\"#/post/676452556\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"564547301","title":"我们不知道如何衡量知识工作者的生产力","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":6,"minutes":1,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · 常青笔记 & 知识工作"},{"id":"574145059","title":"与 Andy Matuschak 畅聊：知识工作、笔记写作和间隔重复","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":68,"minutes":9,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · 常青笔记 & 知识工作"},{"id":"676452556","title":"《辞去你的工作》Wolf Tivy","author":"Wolf Tivy","votes":39,"minutes":6,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"677540148","title":"一些创新洞察依赖于长期记忆","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":19,"minutes":2,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"435560834","title":"头脑风暴往往可以替代缺位的见解积累系统","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":21,"minutes":3,"rea